cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this list in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Awesome Reasoning Models Theory: A theoretical and empirical map of the o-series / R1 / Claude-thinking paradigm"
type: dataset
date-released: 2026-05-14
license: CC0-1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/bettyguo/awesome-reasoning-models-theory"
abstract: >-
  A curated, theory-first map of the literature on why reasoning models work.
  Covers test-time compute scaling, chain-of-thought mechanism, sampling and
  verification, search at inference, RL-for-reasoning, overthinking, faithfulness,
  and theoretical frameworks bridging the empirical observations. Includes
  reproduction notebooks and a living benchmarks tracker.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - chain of thought
  - reasoning
  - test-time compute
  - reinforcement learning
  - process reward models
  - DeepSeek-R1
  - o1
